usb: sunxi udc: route PHY0 to the device controller on sun50iw9

open_usb_clock() switches the shared PHY0 mux (0x5100420 bit 0) to the
device controller only on a list of SoCs that lacks sun50iw9; U-Boot
uses the port as a host and leaves the mux on the EHCI side, so the
UDC came up enabled and armed with the PHY belonging to ehci0.

--- a/drivers/usb/sunxi_usb/udc/sunxi_udc_board.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/sunxi_usb/udc/sunxi_udc_board.c
@@ -113,8 +113,10 @@
 	|| defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN8IW17) || defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN8IW18) \
 	|| defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN8IW16) || defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN8IW19) \
 	|| defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN8IW8) || defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN8IW20)\
-	|| defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN20IW1) || defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN50IW12)
-	/* otg and hci0 Controller Shared phy in SUN50I and SUN8IW10 */
+	|| defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN20IW1) || defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN50IW12) \
+	|| defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN50IW9)
+	/* otg and hci0 Controller Shared phy in SUN50I and SUN8IW10;
+	 * sun50iw9 too, and U-Boot leaves the mux on the hci side */
 	USBC_SelectPhyToDevice(sunxi_udc_io->usb_vbase);
 #endif
 
